PUBLIC RESPONSE: {{1,4},{2,3},{5}}

My reading of the Kao no Sho / Genji Monogatari Kao Zu chart for the standard 54-chapter edition puts Chapter 39, Mikuriya, on the fifth plate of the third group. In that plate the five vertical bars are drawn with three distinct heights: the leftmost bar 1 is level with bar 4, bars 2 and 3 are drawn at the same intermediate height, and bar 5 stands alone at the lowest height. 

So in terms of equal-height equivalence classes the sticks fall into {1,4} together, {2,3} together, and {5} alone. Sorted by the minimum element of each class that is the partition {{1,4},{2,3},{5}}. That is the pattern conventionally reproduced for Mikuriya in the modern transliterations of the incense figures, e.g. the version used in the Kokubungaku series facsimile.

